In full Core the let-bound lambda is closure-converted: a label with no
captures, whose body uses its own argument, and the let has no type. With
the Prelude imported, an integer literal is its fromInteger, which Idris
evaluates while elaborating only below 100: here 100 is still a call, which
idr-eval folds (mlir.check).
CHECK-LABEL: Main.main :
CHECK: let {{[^:=]*}}= \lam{{[0-9]+}}[](
CHECK-SAME: add_Int(#0, {{.*}}fromInteger{{.*}} 100
